//@version=6
// Probe for the closed-trade list limit (upstream issue #84, fixed in PyneCore
// 6.9.3; pinned as a fix by test_134 since the 6.9.4 landing, card #151).
//
// Reversing on every bar books one closed trade per bar, so a long enough run
// pushes more trades through than the list retains. The reference specifies what
// must hold past the limit, and this probe reports each of them:
//
//   strategy.closedtrades             counts "for the whole trading range", not
//                                     just what the list still holds
//   strategy.closedtrades.first_index becomes the index of the oldest REMAINING
//                                     trade
//   closedtrades.*(n)                 stay anchored to the whole range: index 0 is
//                                     evicted (na), first_index is the oldest kept
//
// `real_total` is the control: the win/loss/breakeven counters keep counting past
// the limit, so their sum is what `strategy.closedtrades` must report.
strategy("closed trade list overflow", initial_capital = 10000000,
         default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1)

if bar_index % 2 == 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
else
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)

plot(strategy.closedtrades, "closedtrades")
plot(strategy.wintrades + strategy.losstrades + strategy.eventrades, "real_total")
plot(strategy.closedtrades.first_index, "first_index")
plot(strategy.closedtrades > 0 ? strategy.closedtrades.entry_bar_index(0) : -1.0, "trade0_entry_bar")
plot(strategy.closedtrades > 0 ? strategy.closedtrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.closedtrades.first_index) : -1.0, "oldest_entry_bar")
